<title>UK: IBM unit sets $200 mln August 2001 bond.</title>
<headline>IBM unit sets $200 mln August 2001 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager ABN Amro Hoare Govett.</p>
<p>BORROWER IBM INTERNATIONAL FINANCE</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     6.375     MATURITY    01.AUG.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.239   PAY DATE    01.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     REOFFER    99.864    SPREAD	+27 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	A1	  LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.375     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.375 PCT MAY 2000 TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
